Subject: ALSA: usb-audio: Add jack detection for Razer Barracuda X (2022) dongle

The Razer Barracuda X (2022) 2.4 GHz dongle (1532:0552) is a UAC1 device
without jack detection. The hid-razer-barracuda driver reports the headset's
wireless link as SW_HEADPHONE_INSERT and SW_MICROPHONE_INSERT on a "Headset
Jack" input device below the same USB device. Reuse the DualSense quirk, which
matches that input device by VID:PID and parent chain, to create "Headphone
Jack" and "Headset Mic Jack" controls.

Tested on v7.2.6 with the out-of-tree driver (0.2.0, then named hid-barracuda):
jacks follow headset power, and PipeWire falls back to another output while the
headset is off. The version for submission is upstream/alsa/ in this repository.

diff --git a/sound/usb/mixer_quirks.c b/sound/usb/mixer_quirks.c
index 74d26fd..57b1e8e 100644
--- a/sound/usb/mixer_quirks.c
+++ b/sound/usb/mixer_quirks.c
@@ -4426,6 +4426,8 @@ int snd_usb_mixer_apply_create_quirk(struct usb_mixer_interface *mixer)
 #if IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_INPUT)
 	case USB_ID(0x054c, 0x0ce6): /* Sony DualSense controller (PS5) */
 	case USB_ID(0x054c, 0x0df2): /* Sony DualSense Edge controller (PS5) */
+	/* Headset link reported as jack switches by hid-razer-barracuda */
+	case USB_ID(0x1532, 0x0552): /* Razer Barracuda X (2022) 2.4 GHz dongle */
 		err = snd_dualsense_controls_create(mixer);
 		break;
 #endif /* IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_INPUT) */
